{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An upgrade with an older local-repository run in flight leaves that run unable to resume because its source-owned worktree cannot be registered."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart during baseline gates can leave an existing worktree without the evidence required for recovery, causing resume to fail."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"resume","trigger":"normal","reason":"An installation that continues running the old release after the fixed cutoff can create worktrees that fail recovery on a later upgrade."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A resumed run waiting for human review can be reported as failed when the earlier Git probe encounters a trust error."},{"id":"C3b","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A later failed prepare attempt can exclude an older unrecorded worktree from recovery, leaving the run unable to resume."}]}